--!strict
--[[
	Types — the single import point for cross-module types (ARCHITECTURE §4).

	Purpose:          `local Types = require("@game/ReplicatedStorage/Shared/Types")` then `Types.World`, `Types.Result<T>`.
	Dependencies:     Types/Core, World, Adapters, Net, Service, Content, Battle, Profile (all type-only).
	State:            None.
	Validation:       N/A.
	Error handling:   N/A.
	Performance notes: Erased at runtime; the module value is an empty frozen table.

	Adding a type: declare it in the domain module (Types/<Domain>.luau). During parallel work, teams import their
	domain module directly (`require("@game/ReplicatedStorage/Shared/Types/Combat")`) and do NOT edit this file; the
	lead consolidates re-exports here after each wave. Domain modules must only require other Types modules (never
	implementation modules) so no require cycle can form.
]]

